# novggt_qwen35_4b_reason190k_mixv2_1 (mix-v2-1): video + scene on rows whose needed labels are fully or partially in the
# 31 detector classes; video only on all other rows and on every appearance-order, route-planning and room-size row.
# Scene = the VGG-T-Det (ESL31) boxes for 2/3 of those rows and the GT boxes of the covered labels (score 1.0) for 1/3.
# Every box has a score; prompt: trust each box according to its score; no scene -> answer from the video alone.
# ScanNet++ has detector output for 242 of its 839 scenes (poses of the rest not transferred yet): the others are video only.
# Data: data/reason190k_videoscene_det/build_mix.py (mix-v2 line in its docstring) -> data/reason190k_mixv2_1_answer.jsonl.gz
# Inference: detector scene (with scores) on fully covered questions, video only elsewhere.
# Otherwise as novggt_qwen35_4b_reason190k_vs: --arch none, LoRA r64/a128, lr 1e-4, 1 fps <=64 frames, plain prompt,
# thinking off, bare answer, 1 epoch at global batch 256 (569 steps).
VGGT_ARGS=(--video_fps 1.0 --video_max_frames 64)
MIX=reason190k_mixv2_1
MODEL_ARGS=(--model_name_or_path Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B --arch none --prompt plain)
TRAIN_ARGS=(--learning_rate 1e-4 --lora_r 64 --lora_alpha 128 --dataloader_num_workers 8
  --checkpoint_above 8192)
# Gradient checkpointing only for micro-batches over 8,192 tokens (96 GB cards); wukong (46 GB) passes --checkpoint_above 4500.
GRAD_CKPT=True
EVAL_ARGS=(--max_new_tokens 16)
